# Pi Tool Guidance

## Runtime Permissions

Use the active tool definitions and enforced permissions.
This repository does not explicitly register the previously documented `/perm` extension.
Do not assume its commands, mode settings, or sensitive-path blocks exist.
Verify runtime protection before relying on it; written safety rules are not an enforcement mechanism.

# AI Dotfiles Source of Truth

Edit AI-agent configuration in `~/.local/share/chezmoi-ai`, or its active worktree.
Do not edit generated destinations under `~/.pi/`, `~/.codex/`, or `~/.config/`.
Preview the affected destinations, then run `mise run apply -- --exclude=scripts <destination>...` from that checkout.
Bare `mise apply` applies all configuration and eligible installation scripts; use it only when requested.
Follow the active user and repository commit policy.

## zg (zvec-grep)

The zvec-grep MCP search tool runs indexed semantic search (transport: `zg server --stdio`, per `mcp.json`). Routing rules live in `<exploration_gate>` above — this block covers Pi specifics only.

- Semantic discovery → MCP search with `{"root":"<absolute workspace>","query":"<question>"}` (multi-angle: `queries: [...]`, single ranked list: `fuse: true`).
- Exact words, identifiers, paths, regex → `zg query --rg <pattern>` via bash (no index needed).
- If MCP is unavailable, use `zg query "<question>"` for semantic discovery.
- Follow the shared index lifecycle policy. Reuse existing background refreshes.
- A sufficient, current snippet counts as read evidence. Confirm uncertain snippets against current files.

## codemode

When Pi `codemode` is available, prefer it over separate tool calls: batch independent calls into one call (`Promise.allSettled`), chain dependent ones, filter large output in-script. Check exit codes; do not hide relevant output. Sequential steps (staging, commits) stay sequential — stop at the first failure.